This file gathers and re-exports the index-set reencoding and its membership, self-membership, inclusion, intersection, and zero laws, the embedded sequence and its zero, master, emptiness, nonemptiness, and neighbourhood laws, the transfer of inclusions and equalities, the neighbourhood system generated by the embedded sequence and the subsystem relation, the two element maps, and the order isomorphism. The module comment records the first sentence of Theorem 8.8: an arbitrary enumeration is reindexed by the down-sets of indices, with master the set of all indices, so that inclusions of index sets match inclusions of enumerated neighbourhoods and a witnessed intersection in the original system supplies the intersection law of the embedded system.
